FIVE DEEP-THINKING LENSES
(Apply all five to every significant bug you find)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

LENS 1 — THE STRANDED-FUNDS LENS
  "Could this bug cause SOL or tokens to be permanently
  unrecoverable — even if the user refreshes or retries?"
  Stranded-funds bugs are the highest severity because they
  have no recovery path. Ask this for every transaction,
  every sweep, every sell, every redistribution.

LENS 2 — THE SILENT-FAILURE LENS
  "Could this bug produce a wrong result with no error,
  no console log, and no visible sign to the user?"
  Silent failures are deadlier than crashes. A crash tells
  the user something went wrong. A silent failure lets them
  believe everything is fine while their position is open,
  their sweep returned nothing, or their SOL is draining.

LENS 3 — THE WORST-CASE-RESUME LENS
  "What is the worst possible state this could be in after
  a page reload — tab crash — browser kill — network loss?"
  For every piece of state, ask: if the process died right
  here, what would _resumeActive find, and would it do the
  right thing?

LENS 4 — THE OLD-RECORD LENS
  "What happens if this code runs against a deployment
  record created 10 versions ago, before this field
  existed?"
  Fields added in later releases are undefined in old
  records. Every read of a stored field needs a sane
  default or it becomes the root cause of a class of bugs
  that is incredibly hard to reproduce in development but
  triggers reliably for users who have been using the app
  for a while.

LENS 5 — THE CONCURRENT-ACTION LENS
  "What happens if two things happen simultaneously that
  the developer assumed would be sequential?"
  Organic trigger fires + user clicks Sell Now.
  Page becomes visible + trigger fires during the 2s timer.
  Wallet regeneration during a recirculation pass.
  Two rapid launchToken calls from double-click.
  Every shared guard (in-progress flags, session maps)
  must be set BEFORE the first await, not after.

