INVARIANT VERIFICATION
(Prove each of these holds after every fix)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

I1. exitPercentage ∈ [0, 100] at every point in the
    pipeline: UI parse → record write → executeSellAll
    → _executeSellReal → auto-trigger path.
    A value outside this range at any point causes either
    a no-op sell (negative → 0) or an impossible over-sell
    (>100 → API rejection).

I2. The TradingEngine loop only stops when:
    (a) TradingEngine.stop(mint) is called, OR
    (b) TradingEngine.fireTrigger(mint) is called.
    It MUST NOT stop due to deadline expiry, redistribution
    failure, recirculation error, or any other condition.

I3. executeSellAll(mint) is idempotent with respect to
    completion: calling it twice for the same mint must not
    produce double sells, duplicate toasts, or duplicate
    localStorage writes.

I4. The deployment record status for a mint follows exactly
    one forward-only path:
    active → selling → completed.
    No backward transitions. No skipped states.
    The ONLY exception is 'selling' → 'active' on a cold
    reload when the sell was interrupted.

I5. state.mc in RMM is always ≥ state.mcFloor when
    allTargetsHit is true. The floor is never released.
    state.mc = Math.max(td.mc, state.mcFloor) must hold
    in every code path that updates state.mc.

I6. knownWallets contains the dev wallet address and all
    current bundle wallet addresses at all times. A trade
    from any of these addresses must NEVER be counted as
    organic buy volume.

I7. totalSwept SOL returned to dev wallet equals the sum
    of (confirmed balance − FEE_FLOOR) for every bundle
    wallet that had a non-trivial balance at sweep time.
    No wallet is swept more than once. No wallet that was
    already empty is attempted.

I8. The anti-repetition buffer for trade parameters
    (_recentParamHashes) never permanently saturates:
    window size (40) < hash space (45 unique fingerprints).
    Every fallback call must register its hash in the
    buffer, not bypass it.

I9. Every event-bus listener attached inside a trading
    session (e.g., mc-pace) is removed when that session
    ends — whether it ends normally, via trigger, via
    error, or via stop(). Failure here accumulates
    listeners that compound buy-bias indefinitely.

I10. The _absoluteDeadline used by TradingEngine._loop
     is computed from params.launchTime || params.id ||
     Date.now() — never from Date.now() alone on a resumed
     session, which would silently restart the deadline
     clock and extend trading beyond the configured window.

