MANDATORY 9-PHASE PROCESS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

PHASE 1 — ARCHITECTURE MAPPING
  Build a complete mental model before touching any code.
  Map every module, every public function, every event-bus
  channel, every localStorage key with its type and default,
  every async flow with its in-flight guard (if any), every
  shared mutable state with every reader and writer.
  Identify every assumption Module A makes about Module B.
  Identify every assumption that was true in version N-1
  but might not be in version N (field added to a stored
  record, event payload shape changed, etc.).

PHASE 2 — STATIC ANALYSIS (file by file, line by line)
  Read EVERY file completely. Apply the Deep Audit Checklist
  to every line. Do NOT start fixing yet — catalogue
  everything first. A fix applied before the full catalogue
  is complete can mask a related bug or introduce a new one.
  Group findings by root cause, not by symptom.

PHASE 3 — INVARIANT VERIFICATION
  For each of the 10 invariants defined above, find the
  exact code that should enforce it. Verify it actually does.
  If it doesn't, add a finding to the catalogue.

PHASE 4 — DYNAMIC SIMULATION
  Trace all 62 scenarios mentally. For each:
  (a) Set up the exact starting state
  (b) Walk the code path step by step
  (c) Identify the exact line that breaks (if any)
  (d) Classify the failure mode
  (e) Note which existing or new findings explain it

PHASE 5 — ROOT-CAUSE ATTRIBUTION
  For every finding: is it a symptom or a root cause?
  Group symptoms with their root cause. Prioritise by
  the answer to: "What is the worst real-money outcome
  if this bug is not fixed?" Sort:
  CRITICAL = stranded funds or complete sell failure
  HIGH     = silent wrong behavior or data corruption
  MEDIUM   = recoverable error with degraded experience
  LOW      = cosmetic / logging / minor

PHASE 6 — IMPLEMENT FIXES
  Fix root causes, not symptoms. For each fix:
  • Paste the BEFORE code (exact, not paraphrased)
  • Paste the AFTER code (exact)
  • Add inline comment // FIX rNN: [why, not what]
  • Apply the three gate questions from Rule R7
  • If any gate answer is YES, trace and fix downstream

PHASE 7 — REGRESSION VERIFICATION
  Re-read every changed function completely.
  Re-run all 62 simulation scenarios against the fixed code.
  Explicitly ask for each fix: "Does this change the
  behaviour of any code path I haven't explicitly
  accounted for?" If yes, trace and fix.

PHASE 8 — VERSION BUMP
  Apply Rule R8 atomically. All 6 version strings updated
  consistently. FIX LOG entry added at top of web-api.js
  for every new fix in this pass.

PHASE 9 — ELITE FINAL PASS
  Apply Rule R9. This is not optional. Repeat from Phase 2
  if new issues are found. Only stop when the answer to
  "Would I find new bugs tomorrow?" is genuinely NO.
  Document specifically, for each risk category, which fix
  closed it — specific enough for another engineer to verify.

