  An anti-repetition buffer window larger than the hash space
  saturates after N unique values and forces EVERY subsequent
  call to the fallback. The fallback produces repeating patterns.
  Window > hash space = permanently broken uniqueness guarantee.
  Seen in: _recentDelayBuckets (window 40 → 4), _recentBuyPctBuckets
