FIVE DEEP-THINKING LENSES  (apply all to every significant bug)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

LENS 1 — STRANDED FUNDS
  "Could this bug permanently prevent SOL or tokens from being
  recovered, even if the user refreshes or retries?"
  Stranded funds have no recovery path. Ask for every transaction,
  every sweep, every sell, every redistribution. Even a "temporary"
  strand is critical if the user has no visible way to detect it.

LENS 2 — SILENT FAILURE
  "Could this produce a wrong result with NO error, NO console log,
  and NO visible change to the user?"
  Sells that send '0%'. Sweeps that return nothing. Triggers that
  fire but sell nothing because exitPercentage clamped to 0. A
  user who sees all the right toasts while their position is still open.

LENS 3 — WORST-CASE RESUME
  "What is the absolute worst state this could be in after a tab
  crash, browser kill, or network loss at the WORST possible moment?"
  For every piece of mutable state, ask: if the process died right here,
  what would _resumeActive find, and what would it do?

LENS 4 — OLD-RECORD COMPATIBILITY
  "What if this code runs against a deployment record created 20
  versions ago, before this field existed?"
  Every field read from a stored record needs a safe default. undefined
  fields are the single largest source of NaN propagation in this codebase.

LENS 5 — CONCURRENT ACTION
  "What if two things happen simultaneously that were assumed sequential?"
  Organic trigger fires + user clicks Sell Now.
  visibilitychange fires during the 2s trigger-to-sell window.
  Wallet regeneration during a recirculation sell pass.
  Two rapid Launch clicks from different browser tabs.
  Every shared guard must be set BEFORE the first await.

